  "name": "Example: The Quotient Rule With Cube Roots",
  "problem": "Express $\\dfrac{\\sqrt[3]{3}}{\\sqrt[3]{4}}$ as a single radical.",
  "worked_solution": "Applying the quotient rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\sqrt[3]{3}}{\\sqrt[3]{4}} = \\sqrt[3] {\\dfrac{3}{4}} .\n$$",
